        {
            "block_label": "figure_title",
            "block_content": "<div style=\"text-align: center;\">Table 2: The Stage 0–10 pipeline with inserted sub-stages 2a, 3b, and 7b. Each stage writes a named output file; gates and scheduled human checkpoints (HiL) attach after the stages indicated. HiL-4, fixing the equilibrium concept, is the only unconditional hard stop tied to a substantive modeling choice (P3); any negative gate verdict creates a separate conditional pause for adjudication. Stage 7b is entered only if the researcher approves a numerical plan at HiL-N1, with results approved and reviewed at HiL-N2 and HiL-N3. Targets lists the failure modes from Table 1 the stage or its gate primarily intercepts; Stages 0 and 1 are preparatory.</div>\n",
