                    1041.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Economists arrive at theory from different starting points, so four entry modes share one core: Model Extension adds a mechanism to a known canonical model; Phenomenon-to-Model takes an empirical or institutional phenomenon and recommends model families; Model Critique returns a referee-style audit of an existing draft; Full Pipeline proceeds from intuition to manuscript skeleton. The orchestration core selects the mode and decomposes theory development into inspectable decisions: what is the puzzle, which model family applies, which institutional facts need checking, which assumptions do the work. That decomposition is what lets gates and checkpoints act on the process itself, at every intermediate step.",
            "block_bbox": [
                137,
                1059,
                1085,
                1215
            ],
            "block_id": 7,
            "block_order": 4,
            "group_id": 7,
